### Streams — asserting a download an action returns
###
### This file lints cleanly with no backend. It demonstrates the `EXPECT Stream.*` subjects.
###
### When a custom action returns a stream (server: `Manager.Current.RegisterStream(...)`), the web client
### automatically performs a follow-up GetStream request and delivers the bytes. The .visc runner mirrors
### that: after such an ACTION it auto-fetches the stream and buffers it, so you can assert the observable
### result without any extra verb — exactly as a browser user would experience the download.
###
###   • EXPECT Stream            — presence (IS NULL / IS NOT NULL); no stream captured yet / one was
###   • EXPECT Stream.Name        — the delivered file name
###   • EXPECT Stream.Length      — the byte length (numeric ops)
###   • EXPECT Stream.Text        — the bytes decoded as UTF-8 (CONTAINS / MATCHES / =)
###
### Like the per-verb ClientOperation buffer, the capture reflects only the immediately preceding verb —
### the next executable verb clears it. A server-side download fault (e.g. a missing blob) is served as the
### stream BODY, not a transport error, so its text is assertable via Stream.Text too.
###
### The live round-trip is covered by Vidyano.Script.IntegrationTests (StreamTests), whose in-process model
### returns a RegisteredStream from a DownloadSpec action and serves the bytes via OnGetStream.

@app = "https://demo.vidyano.com"

SIGN-IN admin / admin

### Run an action that returns a downloadable stream; the runner auto-fetches it. No frame is pushed — the
### PO the action ran on stays current.
OPEN MenuItem Products
OPEN-ROW 0
EXPECT Stream IS NULL              ## nothing fetched yet
ACTION DownloadSpec
EXPECT Stream IS NOT NULL
EXPECT Stream.Name = "spec.txt"
EXPECT Stream.Length > 0
EXPECT Stream.Text CONTAINS "%PDF"

### The capture is per-verb: once another verb runs, the stale stream is gone.
GO-BACK
EXPECT Stream IS NULL

### A server-side download fault arrives as the stream body (the GetStream response), not a transport
### error — so the action still succeeds and the fault text is assertable via Stream.Text.
OPEN-ROW 0
ACTION DownloadMissing
EXPECT Stream.Text MATCHES "could not be found"
